- ares is vendored unmodified as the submodule extern/ares under the ISC
  licence (see extern/ares/LICENSE). It carries third-party components of its
  own under their own terms, notably sljit (BSD-2-Clause) and TZXFile (MIT).

- angrylion's Reality Display Processor is vendored unmodified as the submodule
  extern/angrylion-rdp. It descends from MESS and is under the MAME licence
  (see extern/angrylion-rdp/mylittle-nocomment/"MAME License.txt"):
  redistribution is permitted, SALE AND COMMERCIAL USE ARE NOT.

- tests/content/ holds Nintendo 64 test ROMs from PeterLemon/N64, which is
  released under the Unlicense (public domain). See tests/content/README.md.

- BUILT ARTIFACTS (core.wbx and the core package) combine this repository's code
  with ares and with angrylion's RDP, and inherit the latter's terms - in
  particular the NON-COMMERCIAL restriction. ISC and MIT both permit that
  combination; the result may be redistributed freely but not sold.

